course: dictionary
lesson: 3567
title: A word from the farm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fertiliser is something added to soil to help plants grow. Plants take food from the soil, and fertiliser gives them more. «Farmers spread manure and slurry, a runny mix of muck and water, on fields as fertiliser.» The words spread on fields tell you where it goes and why: it helps the crops grow.
explain: Context can show you what a word is made of. «Winter muck becomes spring fertiliser» tells you that animal muck can be turned into fertiliser, and that the cycle starts again each year. If a word sits next to plants, soil or fields, it is probably about growing things.
explain: Some clues give a warning. «Too much washed into rivers harms fish» shows that fertiliser can cause harm when there is too much of it. Ask yourself: what would this word do in the sentence? Then check your idea against the rest of the sentence.
fact: A fertiliser is a substance added to soil to help plants grow.
fact: Manure, compost and chemical pellets can all be fertilisers.
fact: «Bird droppings piled up for centuries on islands were once mined as a rich fertiliser.»
fact: Too much fertiliser can wash into rivers and harm fish and plants.
fact: Keep garden fertiliser away from children and pets. In American English it is spelled fertilizer.
exercise: «Farmers spread manure and slurry on fields as fertiliser.» What is a fertiliser? | *Something added to soil to help plants grow | Something that keeps fish alive in rivers | A kind of seed that never grows | A machine that cuts grass
exercise: In «winter muck becomes spring fertiliser», what does the muck become? | Grass for the summer | *Fertiliser for the spring | Rain for the river | A new farm
exercise: «Bird droppings piled up for centuries on islands were once mined as a rich fertiliser.» Find and copy one word that tells you the fertiliser was valuable. | *rich | islands | droppings | centuries
test: Why should garden fertiliser be kept away from pets? | Because it smells of roses | Because it turns into a toy | Because pets need it to grow | *Because it can harm them
test: How is the American spelling of fertiliser written? | *fertilizer | fertilise | fertiliser the American way | fertilyser
exam: Using the clue «spread on fields», what is fertiliser used for? | Keeping birds away from farms | Making rivers fuller | *Helping crops grow | Washing the tractor
